{"name":"Peppermint Twist","hex":"#96ced5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peppermint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hybrid herb of the mint family (Mentha × piperita), formed by crossing watermint and spearmint, which has a high menthol content and a sharp flavor and is used in cooking, especially in herb teas and in confections. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any of various eucalypts of southeastern Australia whose leaves yield peppermint-like essential oils."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peppermint"},{"term":"twist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A twisting force.","Anything twisted, or the act of twisting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn the ends of something, usually thread, rope etc., in opposite directions, often using force.","To join together by twining one part around another."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peppermint Twist","blocks":[{"text":"\"Peppermint Twist\" is a song written by Joey Dee and Henry Glover, recorded and released by Joey Dee and the Starliters in 1961. Capitalizing on the Twist dance craze and the nightclub in which Dee performed, the song hit No.1 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 in early 1962. It replaced Chubby Checker's \"The Twist\", the song that sparked the Twist fad, at the No. 1 position."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Peppermint_Twist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppermint_Twist","wikidata":"Q7166430"},{"title":"Peppermint Twist (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Peppermint Twist is a New Zealand television series that aired on Two beginning in 1987. With a large focus on music it centres around teenagers in the small New Zealand town of Roseville."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppermint_Twist_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q141435457"},{"title":"Peppermint","blocks":[{"text":"Peppermint is a hybrid species of mint, a cross between watermint and spearmint. Indigenous to Europe and the Middle East, the plant is now widely spread and cultivated in many regions of the world. It is occasionally found in the wild with its parent species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Pfefferminze_natur_peppermint.jpg/330px-Pfefferminze_natur_peppermint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppermint","wikidata":"Q156037"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Mentha-piperita.JPG/500px-Mentha-piperita.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Mentha-piperita.JPG/500px-Mentha-piperita.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peppermint flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMentha-piperita.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg/330px-Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg/330px-Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An 1887 illustration from Köhlers; Medicinal Plants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/From_%27Street_Life_in_London%27%2C_1877%2C_by_John_Thomson_and_Adolphe_Smith_%285780910909%29.jpg/500px-From_%27Street_Life_in